content:
As each window closes (boundary confirmed), the per-beat stream accumulated during the window is condensed:

```
PerWindowMetrics (computed by 03-heart-metrics-and-events.md)
├── hr: { mean, median, p10, p90, min, max, trend_slope, stability }
├── hrv: { rmssd, sdnn, pnn50, dc, ac, sd1, sd2 }
├── morphology: { pr_median, qrs_median, qtc_median, pr_variability, qrs_variability, qtc_variability }
├── rhythm: { beat_type_counts, ectopic_fraction, pause_count, longest_pause_ms }
├── respiration: { edr_rate, edr_variability }
├── events: [ list of flagged episodes within this window ]
└── extremes: { min_hr, max_hr, longest_rr, shortest_rr }
```

The raw beats JSONL file is retained on disk and not deleted. Windows contain **summary statistics**, not raw beats. This keeps the timeline lightweight — a day with 100 windows (~100-1000 rows depending on activity) is a few kilobytes of JSON.

```json
{
  "moments": [
    {
      "type": "hr_peak",
      "start_elapsed_ms": 55812000,
      "duration_s": 12,
      "peak_hr": 143,
      "baseline_hr_p95": 138,
      "notability": "interesting"
    },
    {
      "type": "vagal_rebound",
      "start_elapsed_ms": 55824000,
      "detail": "After the active window, your heart rate settled below usual and HRV rose above your typical range",
      "notability": "interesting"
    }
  ],
  "moment_summary": {
    "total_moments": 2,
    "categories": {
      "effort_achievement": 1,
      "rhythm_pattern": 0,
      "adaptation_recovery": 1
    },
    "moment_types": ["hr_peak", "vagal_rebound"]
  }
}
```

Dotted oval platform (Canvas dash stroke) + the **real Rive heart avatar** (`heart_avatar.riv`, loaded from `res/raw`). The artboard **`Artboard`** and state machine **`State Machine 1`** play with **`ViewModel1`** data binding: the `bpm` number property is set from live HR when connected, otherwise today's average/resting HR from the daily summary, else 72 bpm resting default. Runtime pinned to `app.rive:rive-android:11.6.1` (11.7.0+ blank-render regression, [rive-app/rive-android#459](https://github.com/rive-app/rive-android/issues/459)); the `Rive()` composable fills the stage Box with `Fit.Contain()`.

**State contract (hooks for future data binding):**

```kotlin
enum class BodyState {
    Neutral, Resting, Focused, Active, Recovering, Elevated, Unknown
}
enum class MeasurementState {
    Idle, Connecting, Measuring, Paused
}
```

The app passes `bodyState`, `measurementState`, and `heartRateBpm` into `RiveStage`; `bodyState`/`measurementState` remain reserved for future binding, while `heartRateBpm` drives `ViewModel1.bpm` today.
